      },
      "text": "21 December: Santiago – San Pedro de Atacama – Bolivia"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "87ae06bf2b4771a0109384fea4f8fca5cce37dccc13da90ca7f6104d90662bfa",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-mwa5muwazo597oeipo",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Leave early for the airport and fly to the San Pedro de Atacama area.\n\nThe route then heads to the Bolivian border, where the 4x4 expedition begins.\n\nThe scenery changes dramatically as the city gives way to desert plateaus, volcanoes and high-altitude lagoons.\n\nThe first major natural sight is Laguna Verde.\n\nIn strong winds the water changes from turquoise to emerald green. This is attributed to minerals in the water, including sulfur, lead, arsenic and calcium.\n\nThe Licancabur volcano, around 4,000 m high, rises behind the lagoon. It is considered sacred because objects associated with Inca burial practices have been found in the area.\n\nThe route continues through the Salvador Dalí Desert, named for the surreal shapes of its landscape.\n\nThe next stop is the Polques hot springs, where you can bathe in the hot water.\n\nThen visit the Sol de Mañana geothermal field, with its boiling mud pools and constant emissions.\n\nThe last major stop of the day is Laguna Colorada, known for its reddish water and large numbers of pink flamingos.\n\nAfter the excursion, transfer to Tayka del Desierto."
    },
